35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data confirms my fear. Nine non-joiners refused a full-year commitment. Three quiet members feel uneasy about per-event costs. We need flexibility.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The ledger shows fixed costs dominate. But the hours reveal the real killer: chasing individual payments takes six hours monthly. We must avoid that administrative nightmare.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The sign-in sheets show a quarter of members account for two-thirds of attendances. Eighteen names appear nowhere. The work is carried by the same nine.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The hesitation is real. People stopped treating evenings as theirs once costs became visible. We need a structure that feels like belonging, not a transaction.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, six hours chasing payments? That’s why the account looks thin. I found a third of renewals needed reminders. We need a system that doesn’t rely on begging people for money.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, chasing payments destroys the low-pressure culture. We need a flat fee that removes the anxiety of individual accounting, allowing newcomers to drift in without scrutiny.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, I agree. A flat fee eliminates the six-hour monthly chase. It protects the next treasurer from burnout and keeps the books simple.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
